==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|ars|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{recons|arsaz|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{recons|h₃érsos|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|orso-||behind, arse|lang=ine-pro}}. Compare Dutch {{term|aars|lang=nl}}, English {{term|arse|lang=en}}, Norwegian {{term|rass|lang=no}}.

